  ('STA 311', 'Probability V', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Mathematics', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective. Probability Generating function. Bivariate Normal distribution: conditional and marginal densities, bivariate moment generating functions, characteristic function and inversion formula. Various modes of convergence. Central limit theorem. Elements of measure. Field of sets, fields, measure functions, probability measure and probability space. Introduction to Markov chains: basic concepts, state and parameter space, transition probabilities.', '["Probability Generating function", "Bivariate Normal distribution: conditional and marginal densities, bivariate moment generating functions, characteristic function and inversion formula", "Various modes of convergence", "Central limit theorem", "Elements of measure", "Field of sets, fields, measure functions, probability measure and probability space", "Introduction to Markov chains: basic concepts, state and parameter space, transition probabilities"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mathematics course module'),
  ('STA 321', 'Distribution Theory', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Mathematics', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective. Bivariate Normal Distribution, the gamma, chi-square, two types of Beta, $F$ and $t$ distributions. Distribution of functions of random variables: sums, products and quotients. Probability integral transformation. Order statistics and their functions.', '["Bivariate Normal Distribution, the gamma, chi-square, two types of Beta, $F$ and $t$ distributions", "Distribution of functions of random variables: sums, products and quotients", "Probability integral transformation", "Order statistics and their functions"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mathematics course module'),
  ('STA 331', 'Statistical Inference IV', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Mathematics', '300 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective. Criteria of Estimation: unbiasedness, consistency, efficiency, sufficiency and minimum variance, with proofs. Rao-Cramer Inequality. Testing of hypothesis: Null and alternative hypothesis, simple, composite hypothesis. Two types of error, critical region, Power size of a test, p-value, Neyman-Pearson Theorem. Most powerful test, and likelihood ratio test.', '["Criteria of Estimation: unbiasedness, consistency, efficiency, sufficiency and minimum variance, with proofs", "Rao-Cramer Inequality", "Testing of hypothesis: Null and alternative hypothesis, simple, composite hypothesis", "Two types of error, critical region, Power size of a test, p-value, Neyman-Pearson Theorem", "Most powerful test, and likelihood ratio test"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mathematics course module'),
